mber of days late. It now multiplies the two.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned `n + 1` events because of a slice off-by-one. It now returns exactly `n`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books` was missing the third title. I added `Emma` by Austen, 1815, 1 copy. The author, year and copy count were my guess, since the tests only check the title.\n\u001b[0m\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9b135e14ffemUq084Bb1F6CCv type=finish-step part\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +0ms service=bus type=message.part.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +1ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9b135e14ffemUq084Bb1F6CCv type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +5ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9b135e14ffemUq084Bb1F6CCv sessionID=ses_e9b135e14ffemUq084Bb1F6CCv unlocking\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes: 16 tests, all OK. I changed only files in `catalog/` and left the tests alone.\n\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` left the year as a string. It now converts it to an int.\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3. It is now 5, matching the lending-policy comment and the tests.\n- **`fees.py`:** `late_fee` added the daily fee to the number of days late. It now multiplies the two.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned `n + 1` events because of a slice off-by-one. It now returns exactly `n`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books` was missing the third title. I added `Emma` by Austen, 1815, 1 copy. The author, year and copy count were my guess, since the tests only check the title.INFO  2026-10-22T18:43:22 +2ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_request